  "action": "CE event-stream delivery semantics pass (brief sections 1-20): audited all 7 event types into a FACT/INTERNAL ontology and found world.boundary_signal was engine scheduling detail not a world fact (10 of 21 events, would have frozen the quota mechanism into the public contract); chose at-least-once delivery and documented why exactly-once is impossible at the CE boundary; separated eventId from deliverySequence and attempt; built DeliveryState entirely outside WorldState with cursors, gap detection and state-sync resync; per-tick canonical total order with region-before-source; coalescing for delta facts only, never written back to record or provenance; reference-based causal attribution honest under eviction. TWO ARCHITECTURAL CORRECTIONS: (1) event ids were a bare counter living in WorldState, so two forks of one checkpoint minted IDENTICAL ids for different facts (3/3 collisions measured) - now SHA-256 over timeline+tick+ordinal+content, probed BEFORE designing delivery because id-based dedup on non-unique ids would have been unimplementable; (2) moved events OUT of stateHash and dynamics INTO it, correcting section 18.4 - the event buffer is a record of facts (history) not a delivery obligation, and timeline-scoped ids in stateHash broke branch convergence. 255 tests pass (54 new), tsc clean. Verdict ACCEPTED WITH CAVEATS; contract stable enough to design the adapter API except for event retention policy"
